<Layout title="Privacy" description="How information submitted through Wharton Chan's portfolio enquiry forms is used, and how to keep unnecessary sensitive information out of enquiries."><PageIntro eyebrow="Information & Trust" title="Privacy, in plain language." /><div class="container"><article class="prose"><div class="notice">Launch notice: form submissions are disabled until hosting, delivery, and the privacy contact channel are verified. The owner must confirm retention and processor arrangements before enabling enquiries.</div><h2>What the forms ask for</h2><p>The enquiry forms request contact details and information about a proposed event or educational support. Please do not send medical records, patient information, identity documents, or other sensitive personal records.</p><h2>How enquiry information is used</h2><p>Information is used to respond to and manage your enquiry. For full-band performance enquiries, relevant event and contact details may be shared with The Marmalade Jammers leadership team to coordinate arrangements, with your consent.</p><h2>Hosting and form processing</h2><p>When enabled, forms are intended to be processed through Netlify Forms. Hosting and form processing may involve storage outside Singapore. Processor arrangements and an appropriate retention period must be confirmed by the owner before launch. Information should be limited to what is necessary and removed when no longer needed for the enquiry or applicable obligations.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You may ask about access, correction, or deletion of your enquiry information through the professional contact channel once it is published. The verified privacy contact address is awaiting owner confirmation; forms remain disabled in the meantime.</p><h2>Embedded media</h2><p>No analytics or advertising trackers are configured. If YouTube videos are later added, they use YouTube's privacy-enhanced embed domain. Loading or playing embedded content can still share technical information with the provider. Locally hosted media does not require an external video provider.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Contact channels <svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13L13 3M3 3H13V13" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" /></svg></a></article></div></Layout>
